  "close_rendering": "And he was pierced from our transgressions, crushed from our iniquities. The chastisement of our peace was upon him, and by his wound there was healing for us.",
  "whats_happening": "A group speaking as 'we' describes what happened to someone they call 'him'. The whole verse rests on the contrast between them. Every wrongdoing is 'ours', and every suffering is 'his'. The Hebrew links them with one small word, מִן, which can mean 'because of' or 'away from'. Much of how the verse has been read depends on that word.",
  "key_words": [
    {
      "surface": "מְחֹלָ֣ל",
      "lemma": "חָלַל",
      "gloss": "pierced",
      "note": "Describes something done to him. The word covers both piercing and being fatally wounded.",
      "strongs": "H2490a"
    },
    {
      "surface": "מִפְּשָׁעֵ֔נוּ",
      "lemma": "פֶּשַׁע",
      "gloss": "from our transgressions",
      "note": "מִן, joined to the front, can mean 'because of', 'coming from' or 'away from'. Which one is meant changes what the line says.",
      "strongs": "H6588"
    },
    {
      "surface": "נִרְפָּא",
      "lemma": "רָפָא",
      "gloss": "it was healed",
      "note": "Literally 'it was healed': the healing is stated without naming who is healed.",
      "strongs": "H7495"
    },
    {
      "surface": "וּבַחֲבֻרָת֖וֹ",
      "lemma": "חַבּוּרָה",
      "gloss": "and by his wound",
      "note": "One written word carrying four morphemes: conjunction, preposition, noun in construct, and a third person suffix.",
      "strongs": "H2250"
    }
  ],
  "translation_note": "English versions translate מִן differently: 'for', 'because of' or 'from' our transgressions. Each is a fair reading of the Hebrew, but they do not say the same thing.",
